Subject: [PATCH 5/8] 5.0.0 draft, LOCAL ONLY: Step-Tracking's Nested Steps
 says a composite step's sub-steps are drawn the first time it opens, and how
 to draw them all (REPORT_FORMAT_PLAN R5)

---
 Step-Tracking.md | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Step-Tracking.md b/Step-Tracking.md
index 59c2e3a..af47303 100644
--- a/Step-Tracking.md
+++ b/Step-Tracking.md
@@ -261,6 +261,12 @@ public void Setup_database() { /* ... */ }
 public void Seed_test_data() { /* ... */ }
 ```
 
+In the HTML report a step with sub-steps is drawn closed, and opens to show them. From 5.0.0, where its sub-steps come
+to 2 KB of HTML or more, the page holds them compressed and draws them the first time the step is opened, so a suite of
+deeply nested steps keeps a small report. A step on the way to a failure is drawn and open as before. The report's
+search box finds a word in a step nobody opened; the browser's own find (Ctrl+F) does not. Set
+`RenderCollapsedSubStepsOnExpand = false` on `ReportConfigurationOptions` to draw every step. See [[Report Configuration]].
+
